# Canonical identities for git log / shortlog / blame.
#
# Unlike the sibling repos (jax-solitons, jax-morpho, Morphospace), no work address
# has ever landed here: all 14 commits as of 2026-07-31 are authored AND committed as
# jim.galasyn@hotmail.com.
#
# WHY it has not recurred is per-machine, and this comment used to give only the work
# machine's answer as though it were the answer:
#
#   - work machine: a conditional include keyed on the REMOTE URL, so the personal
#     identity attaches to any clone of this repo anywhere on disk —
#       [includeIf "hasconfig:remote.*.url:https://github.com/JimGalasyn/**"]
#               path = ~/.gitconfig-personal
#   - Bender (verified 2026-07-31): no conditional include and no ~/.gitconfig-personal.
#     The global user.email is simply the personal address, and the work address is not
#     configured at all. This checkout ALSO carries a repo-local user.email — which
#     jax-morpho and jax-solitons do not, so do not generalise from it.
#
# Neither is enforceable by the repo, so a new machine is unguarded until it is set up.
# Check `git config user.email` there before the first commit.
#
# So only one of the two lines below fixes anything today:
#
#   * The NAME split is real: "Jim" (8 commits) and "Jim Galasyn" (6) are the same
#     person, and `git shortlog -sne` reported two authors before this file existed.
#     The second line collapses them.
#   * The confluent.io line is PRECAUTIONARY, not corrective — no commit here has ever
#     carried that address. It used to rest on a prediction: the GitHub account's public
#     email is jim.galasyn@confluent.io, so a squash-merged PR would be re-attributed to
#     it. THAT PREDICTION WAS TESTED THREE TIMES AND FAILED EVERY TIME — Morphospace
#     60b138b (#31, 2026-07-28), jax-solitons 918eda7 (#76, 2026-07-31) and jax-morpho
#     0dc9a3a (#9, 2026-07-31) were all squash-merged with author
#     jim.galasyn@hotmail.com, i.e. the BRANCH commit's author, not the account email.
#
#     The premise is still true and is not what was wrong: `gh api user` really does
#     return the work address. The inference drawn from it does not hold. Those are
#     worth keeping apart, because "the account email is still confluent.io" will go on
#     looking like evidence for a prediction it does not support.
#
#     The line stays, on a weaker and honest basis: it costs nothing, GitHub's
#     attribution is not something this repo controls, and if it ever does start firing,
#     an unmapped address would surface here as a second author immediately. Unlike
#     jax-morpho's and jax-solitons' mapping lines, which are corrective and cover 6 and
#     57 real commits, this one is pure insurance.
#
# Counts above are a snapshot, and they INCLUDE the commit that writes them — the two
# previous versions of this comment each gave the parent's numbers, because they were
# read before committing. Recompute after the fact, not before:
#   git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>

Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@confluent.io>
Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com>
